  <page_number>279</page_number>
  <running_head>INVOCAT. SANCT.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Ligna</catchword>
    <signature>S 4</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>Secreta</i> : Sacrificium, Domine, quod tibi immolamus, placatus intende, ut ab omni nos eruat bellorum nequitiâ, &amp; per vexillum sanctæ crucis filii tui, ad conterendas adversariorum insidias, nos in tuæ protectionis securitate constituat.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>Communio</i> : Per signum crucis de inimicis nostris libera nos Deus noster.</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="1" para="true">CRUCIS EXALTATIO.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">Laudes crucis attollamus.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Nos, q; crucis exultamus</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Speciali gloriâ.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Nam in cruce triumphamus,</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">Hostem verum superamus</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Vitali victoriâ.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">Dulce melos tangat coelos,</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Dulce lignu dulci dignum</l>
    <l n="12" para="true">Canamus melodiâ.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Voci vita non discordet,</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">Dū vox vita nō remordet,</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">Dulcis est symphonia.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Servi crucis cruce laudant,</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Qui per cruce sibi gaudent</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">Vita dari munera.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Dicant omnes, dicat singuli:</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">Ave salus totius seculi,</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Arbor salutifera,</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">O quàm felix, q; praclara</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">Fuit hac salutis ara,</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Rubens agni sanguine.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Agnus sine maculâ,</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">Qui mundavit seculâ</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">Ab antiquo crimine.</l>
    <l n="28" para="true">Hac est scala peccatorum,</l>
    <l n="29" para="true">Per q; Christus rex coelorum</l>
    <l n="30" para="true">Ad se traxit omnia.</l>
    <l n="31" para="true">Forma hac cujus ostendit,</l>
    <l n="32" para="true">Qua terrarū comprehendit</l>
    <l n="33" para="true">Quatuor confinia.</l>
    <l n="34" para="true">Non sunt nova sacramenta,</l>
    <l n="35" para="true">Nec recenter est inventa</l>
    <l n="36" para="true">Crucis hac religio.</l>
    <l n="37" para="true">Ista dulces aquas fecit,</l>
    <l n="38" para="true">Per hanc silex aquas jecit.</l>
    <l n="39" para="true">Moysis officio.</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">Nulla salus est in domo,</l>
    <l n="41" para="true">Nisi cruce munit homo</l>
    <l n="42" para="true">Superliminaria.</l>
    <l n="43" para="true">Neque sensit gladium,</l>
    <l n="44" para="true">Nec amisit filium,</l>
    <l n="45" para="true">Quisquis egit talia.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse printed in two parallel columns; the right column is set after the left, in reading order. Some words in the scan are doubtful and may be misread: "seculâ" and "Dulce lignu" in particular. Several letters of the Latin are blurred by the scan (e.g. "Quatuor", "comprehendit" read from a worn line).</notes>
